# Home Assistant naxsi whitelist - hand-written, NOT a community-
# maintained ruleset (none exists for Home Assistant). Scoped narrowly
# to fix confirmed false positives from real traffic in
# naxsi_error.log; only extend when a new false positive is confirmed
# there, not speculatively.

# Preventive (not log-confirmed): a WAF should never content-scan a
# password field - HA's login flow API uses a JSON "password" field.
# Same reasoning as the other password-field fixes.
BasicRule wl:0 "mz:$BODY_VAR:password";
